{
  "_comment": [
    "Maps an assertion's MESSAGE to the invariant it enforces, so mutation results",
    "can be reconciled against docs/plan/AUDIT_INVARIANTS.md mechanically.",
    "",
    "Keyed on the message, not the line number: line numbers move on every edit and",
    "a stale mapping silently reconciles the wrong row. Messages are stable and are",
    "already required to be distinct enough for a human to debug from.",
    "",
    "An assertion whose message is absent here is UNMAPPED, which the reconciler",
    "reports separately. Unmapped is not benign: it means an assertion enforces",
    "something no invariant claims, i.e. the register may be incomplete. That is",
    "exactly how the cancel path (L5, L6) turned out to be missing."
  ],
